==Enemy==
Despite looking similar, Shy Boy is almost entirely different from [[The Face]]. He moves at '''forty''' times the speed and attacks rapidly, but with less than half the range. He is only around 1/3 as tough compared to The Face, yet dishes out more DPS. Furthermore, his high strength magnifications make him an annoying enemy later in the game. He also has a surprisingly high money drop making it worthwhile to rush him down, especially in stages like [[Volcanic Defender]] where he appears early.

==Strategy==
You can exploit his dual-trait weakness with [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] or [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] attackers that are well rounded in health and attack power. Examples are [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]]. Due to his high money drop, you shouldn't hesitate spending a lot of your budget to defeat him.

Shy Boy is also very vulnerable to status effects like [[Slow|slow]] and freeze, as due to his short range, he barely does anything without his speed advantage. This means that [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Bishop Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hip Hop Cat]] and [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]] can get the job done just fine.

